---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Home — Center for Mesoamerican Studies">
  <script type="module" src="https://unpkg.com/@google/model-viewer/dist/model-viewer.min.js" is:inline></script>

  <section class="hero-shell">
    <div class="page-grid hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Faculty of Arts • Comenius University Bratislava</p>
        <h1>Central Mesoamerican studies built from fieldwork, archives, and living scholarship.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lead">
          The Center for Mesoamerican Studies unites archaeology, epigraphy, history, religion,
          material culture, and digital methods into one research platform. It exists to study,
          publish, teach, and preserve the worlds of ancient Mesoamerica with academic rigor.
        </p>

        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/about-us" class="button button-primary">About institute</a>
          <a href="/grants-and-investigations" class="button button-secondary">Research projects</a>
        </div>

        <dl class="hero-facts">
          <div>
            <dt>Founded</dt>
            <dd>2015</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Flagship fieldwork</dt>
            <dd>PARU Uaxactun since 2016</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Core strength</dt>
            <dd>Research, collections, doctoral support</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-visuals">
        <div class="hero-panel hero-panel-model">
          <div class="panel-topline">Digital archaeology</div>
          <model-viewer
            src="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/VSHT3/MESOAMERICA-ASSETS/main/statue%20compressed.glb"
            camera-controls
            auto-rotate
            auto-rotate-delay="0"
            rotation-per-second="18deg"
            interaction-prompt="none"
            disable-zoom
            camera-orbit="90deg 75deg"
            alt="3D model of a Mesoamerican artefact"
          ></model-viewer>
          <p class="panel-note">3D documentation and object study sit alongside excavation, archives, and teaching.</p>
        </div>

        <figure class="hero-panel hero-panel-image">
          <img
            src="/assets/petnal0084_7cQP6ek3nJnqnU40sK0MD.jpg"
            alt="Reconstruction view of monumental Maya architecture in a rainforest landscape"
            loading="eager"
            decoding="async"
          />
          <figcaption>Reconstruction, landscape interpretation, and site context remain central to CMS research.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-grid intro-ribbon" aria-label="Institute summary">
    <p>
      Founded as a multidisciplinary scientific center, CMS brings together Slovak and international
      specialists working on Maya and Nahua cultures, archaeology, astronomy, manuscripts,
      iconography, religion, and historical thought.
    </p>
    <a href="/publications">Browse publications</a>
  </section>

  <section class="page-grid domains-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Research domains</p>
      <h2>Not one department. An entire knowledge field in conversation.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="domains-list">
      <article>
        <span class="domain-index">01</span>
        <h3>Field archaeology</h3>
        <p>Excavation, landscape study, and ceramic research anchored by long-term work in Petén, Guatemala.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="domain-index">02</span>
        <h3>Epigraphy and manuscripts</h3>
        <p>Maya hieroglyphic writing, codices, Nahuatl sources, and historical records studied with linguistic and philological depth.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="domain-index">03</span>
        <h3>Technology and documentation</h3>
        <p>LiDAR, photogrammetry, RTI, ceramic scanning, and 3D modeling expand how evidence is captured and interpreted.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="domain-index">04</span>
        <h3>Teaching and mentorship</h3>
        <p>Doctoral training, thesis support, consultations, and direct participation in scientific projects shape new specialists.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-grid feature-band">
    <div class="feature-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Flagship achievement</p>
      <h2>PARU Uaxactun gives the institute a visible field presence, not only a library presence.</h2>
      <p>
        Since 2016, the Uaxactun Regional Archaeological Project has been a defining CMS platform for
        excavation, coordination, funding, publication work, and international visibility. It positions
        the center as one of the strongest European research actors in the Maya area.
      </p>
      <a href="/paru-uaxactun-history" class="text-link">Enter PARU Uaxactun</a>
    </div>

    <div class="feature-aside">
      <div class="aside-item">
        <span>2015</span>
        <p>Center established as dedicated multidisciplinary hub.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="aside-item">
        <span>2016</span>
        <p>PARU Uaxactun becomes long-term flagship research platform.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="aside-item">
        <span>Now</span>
        <p>Teaching, collections, exhibitions, conferences, and publications feed one ecosystem.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-grid institute-section">
    <div class="section-heading section-heading-wide">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why this institute matters</p>
      <h2>CMS was built to make Mesoamerican studies visible, serious, and institutionally durable in Central Europe.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="institute-columns">
      <div class="institute-text">
        <p>
          Based at Štúrova 9 within the Faculty of Arts, the center operates as an independent academic
          base with its own research identity. It was created to gather expertise that had previously been
          dispersed across universities and projects.
        </p>
        <p>
          That mission remains intact: connect scholarship, material evidence, and public knowledge. The
          result is a center that supports advanced research while also making room for exhibitions,
          conference activity, specialist libraries, and student formation.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="institute-stack">
        <div>
          <h3>Collections and memory</h3>
          <p>Archaeological and ethnographical collections, the Ferdinand Anders Library, and publication archives extend research beyond the field season.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Contemporary methods</h3>
          <p>Ancient subjects are approached with modern tools, from landscape scanning to object digitization and visual reconstruction.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Scholarly reach</h3>
          <p>The site’s sections on conferences, grants, exhibitions, and publications reflect an institute with active public and academic output.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-grid navigation-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Start here</p>
      <h2>Main paths into the institute.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="navigation-grid">
      <a href="/about-us" class="nav-tile">
        <span>About</span>
        <strong>History, mission, people</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="/publications" class="nav-tile">
        <span>Publications</span>
        <strong>Research output and reports</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="/ferdinand-anders-library" class="nav-tile">
        <span>Library</span>
        <strong>Ferdinand Anders Library</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="/collection-archaeological-collection" class="nav-tile">
        <span>Collections</span>
        <strong>Archaeological and ethnographical holdings</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="/bratislava-maya-meetings-news" class="nav-tile">
        <span>Conferences</span>
        <strong>Bratislava Maya Meetings and updates</strong>
      </a>
      <a href="/education-phd-program" class="nav-tile">
        <span>Education</span>
        <strong>Doctoral pathway and student work</strong>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Marcellus&family=Literata:opsz,wght@7..72,400;7..72,500;7..72,600&display=swap');

  :global(:root) {
    --home-bg-1: oklch(0.18 0.033 206);
    --home-bg-2: oklch(0.14 0.025 202);
    --home-panel: color-mix(in oklab, oklch(0.22 0.028 196) 80%, black);
    --home-panel-soft: oklch(0.25 0.03 188 / 0.46);
    --home-text: oklch(0.9 0.02 92);
    --home-text-dim: oklch(0.77 0.025 186);
    --home-line: oklch(0.43 0.05 182 / 0.45);
    --home-accent: oklch(0.72 0.108 176);
    --home-accent-2: oklch(0.67 0.085 144);
    --home-gold: oklch(0.8 0.09 95);
    --home-shadow: 0 28px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34);
  }

  :global(html),
  :global(body) {
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(41, 141, 129, 0.18), transparent 28%),
      radial-gradient(circle at top right, rgba(28, 87, 110, 0.32), transparent 24%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--home-bg-1) 0%, var(--home-bg-2) 48%, oklch(0.12 0.018 198) 100%);
    color: var(--home-text);
    font-family: 'Literata', Georgia, serif;
  }

  :global(main) {
    overflow: clip;
  }

  .page-grid {
    width: min(1280px, calc(100% - 2rem));
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero-shell {
    padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem) 0 2rem;
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(320px, 0.95fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    align-items: end;
  }

  .hero-copy {
    padding: clamp(1rem, 2vw, 2rem) 0 clamp(1rem, 1vw, 1.5rem);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--home-accent);
  }

  h1,
  h2,
  h3 {
    font-family: 'Marcellus', serif;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(3.4rem, 8vw, 7.2rem);
    line-height: 0.94;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .hero-lead,
  .intro-ribbon p,
  .feature-copy p,
  .institute-text p,
  .institute-stack p,
  .domains-list p,
  .aside-item p {
    max-width: 66ch;
    font-size: 1.03rem;
    line-height: 1.85;
    color: var(--home-text-dim);
  }

  .hero-lead {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    min-height: 3rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--home-line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    transition: transform 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease, background-color 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
  }

  .button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .button-primary {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, color-mix(in oklab, var(--home-accent-2) 72%, black), color-mix(in oklab, var(--home-accent) 76%, black));
    color: oklch(0.97 0.008 120);
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--home-accent) 55%, black);
  }

  .button-secondary {
    color: var(--home-text);
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  }

  .hero-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--home-line);
  }

  .hero-facts div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .hero-facts dt {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--home-accent);
  }

  .hero-facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--home-text);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .hero-visuals {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .hero-panel {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--home-line);
    background:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(18, 54, 58, 0.94), rgba(8, 23, 30, 0.94)),
      var(--home-panel);
    box-shadow: var(--home-shadow);
  }

  .hero-panel-model {
    min-height: 500px;
    padding: 1rem;
    clip-path: polygon(0 0, 100% 0, 100% 88%, 88% 100%, 0 100%);
  }

  .panel-topline {
    position: absolute;
    top: 1rem;
    left: 1rem;
    z-index: 2;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--home-gold);
  }

  .hero-panel-model model-viewer {
    width: 100%;
    height: 420px;
    display: block;
    --poster-color: transparent;
  }

  .panel-note,
  figcaption {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 42ch;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--home-text-dim);
  }

  .hero-panel-image {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.9rem;
    transform: translateX(-10%);
  }

  .hero-panel-image img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    object-fit: cover;
    display: block;
    filter: saturate(0.85) contrast(1.04) brightness(0.78);
  }

  .intro-ribbon,
  .domains-section,
  .feature-band,
  .institute-section,
  .navigation-section {
    padding: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem) 0;
  }

  .intro-ribbon {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) auto;
    gap: 1rem 2rem;
    align-items: center;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--home-line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--home-line);
  }

  .intro-ribbon a,
  .text-link {
    color: var(--home-gold);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .section-heading {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 3rem);
  }

  .section-heading h2,
  .feature-copy h2 {
    max-width: 16ch;
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.3rem);
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  .section-heading-wide h2 {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .domains-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .domains-list article {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.9rem;
    min-height: 240px;
    padding: 1.4rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--home-line);
    background:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(18, 42, 49, 0.88), rgba(8, 20, 26, 0.78)),
      var(--home-panel-soft);
  }

  .domain-index {
    color: var(--home-accent);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  }

  .domains-list h3,
  .institute-stack h3 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.55rem;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }

  .domains-list p,
  .institute-stack p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .feature-band {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(280px, 0.62fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
    align-items: start;
  }

  .feature-aside {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .aside-item {
    padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--home-line);
    background: rgba(4, 16, 21, 0.46);
  }

  .aside-item span {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--home-accent);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .aside-item p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.98rem;
  }

  .institute-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(280px, 0.88fr);
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 4rem);
  }

  .institute-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .institute-stack div {
    padding: 1.15rem 0 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--home-line);
  }

  .navigation-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .nav-tile {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    min-height: 150px;
    padding: 1.2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--home-line);
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(14, 40, 45, 0.68), rgba(6, 14, 18, 0.86));
    transition: transform 180ms ease, border-color 180ms ease, background-color 180ms ease;
  }

  .nav-tile:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px);
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--home-accent) 60%, white 10%);
  }

  .nav-tile span {
    color: var(--home-accent);
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .nav-tile strong {
    color: var(--home-text);
    font-family: 'Marcellus', serif;
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1080px) {
    .hero-grid,
    .feature-band,
    .institute-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .hero-panel-image {
      transform: none;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .page-grid {
      width: min(100% - 1.25rem, 1280px);
    }

    h1 {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 14vw, 4.3rem);
    }

    .hero-facts,
    .domains-list,
    .intro-ribbon {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .section-heading h2,
    .feature-copy h2 {
      max-width: none;
      font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 9vw, 3rem);
    }

    .hero-panel-model {
      min-height: auto;
    }

    .hero-panel-model model-viewer {
      height: 320px;
    }
  }
</style>
